stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NON_BIOMETRIC: joiner or migrated employee, non-biometric by default
    NON_BIOMETRIC --> CONSENTED: employee elects a modality and gives written consent
    CONSENTED --> TICKETED: regime resolved, enrolment ticket issued for named devices
    CONSENTED --> NON_BIOMETRIC: consent withdrawn before a ticket is issued
    TICKETED --> ENROLLED: first enrolment evidence inside the ticket window
    TICKETED --> NON_BIOMETRIC: ticket expires or consent withdrawn before enrolment
    ENROLLED --> ERASING: written withdrawal, method switch, site transfer, modality disabled or exit
    ERASING --> ERASED: every device item confirmed or closed by attestation
    ERASED --> NON_BIOMETRIC: election stays non-biometric, re-enrolment needs a new consent version
    ERASED --> [*]: exit
    NON_BIOMETRIC --> UNTICKETED: biometric punch or template upload with no live ticket
    UNTICKETED --> ERASING: erasure opened for that device, tenant admin alerted
    ERASING --> ERASING: same serial returns after attestation, item reopened
    note right of ENROLLED
        Punches never reference the template.
        The regime is fixed at capture - SPDI
        before the switch date, DPDP after it.
    end note
